					<description><![CDATA[<p><img width="612" height="344" src="https://www.actionforex.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/f-usd224.jpg" class="attachment-post-thumbnail size-post-thumbnail wp-post-image" alt="" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" srcset="https://www.actionforex.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/f-usd224.jpg 612w, https://www.actionforex.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/f-usd224-600x337.jpg 600w, https://www.actionforex.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/f-usd224-150x84.jpg 150w, https://www.actionforex.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/f-usd224-300x169.jpg 300w" sizes="(max-width: 612px) 100vw, 612px" /></p>
<p>TL;DR: The Dollar rally has lost momentum rather than direction. DXY stalled at 102.232 as Fed urgency faded, long-end Treasury yields met buyer demand at two-decade highs, and France was left shouldering more of the Dollar’s remaining support. Absent a sizeable US CPI surprise, the Dollar looks poised for consolidation, with scope to drift lower [&#8230;]</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.actionforex.com/action-insight/market-overview/weekly-report/657142-has-the-dollar-rally-stalled-or-is-it-already-waiting-for-the-midterms/">Has the Dollar Rally Stalled, or Is It Already Waiting for the Midterms?</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.actionforex.com">ActionForex</a>.</p>
]]></description>
		
		
		
